    "## Decoder\n",
    "\n",
    "The decoder generates output tokens one-by-one.\n",
    "\n",
    "It contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Masked Self-Attention\n",
    "2. Encoder-Decoder Attention\n",
    "3. Feed Forward Layers\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why Masking\n",
    "\n",
    "During training: The model should NOT see future words.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"I love deep ...\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "It cannot peek at the next word.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Example Workthrough\n",
    "\n",
    "Let’s translate:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"I love cats\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "to French:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"J'aime les chats\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Input Embedding\n",
    "\n",
    "Words become vectors:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"I\"     → [0.2, 0.1, ...]\n",
    "\"love\"  → [0.5, 0.9, ...]\n",
    "\"cats\"  → [0.8, 0.3, ...]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Add Positional Encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "Now order information is included.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Encoder Attention\n",
    "\n",
    "The word “love” may attend strongly to:\n",
    "\n",
    "* “I”\n",
    "* “cats”\n",
    "\n",
    "to understand context.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Decoder Starts\n",
    "\n",
    "Decoder receives:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "<START>\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Predicts:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"J'\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Next:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"J'aime\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Then:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"les\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Then:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"chats\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Attention Weights\n",
    "\n",
    "Sentence:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"The bank approved the loan because it trusted John.\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "When processing “it”:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Word | Attention |\n",
    "| ---- | --------- |\n",
    "| bank | 0.75      |\n",
    "| loan | 0.10      |\n",
    "| John | 0.15      |\n",
    "\n",
    "The model learns:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"it\" → bank\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Charecterstics\n",
    "\n",
    "### Complexity\n",
    "\n",
    "Self-attention complexity:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "O(n^2)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "because every word compares with every other word, which becomes expensive for long sequences.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "| Advantage          | Why Important            |\n",
    "| ------------------ | ------------------------ |\n",
    "| Parallelization    | Much faster training     |\n",
    "| Long-range context | Better understanding     |\n",
    "| Scalable           | Works with huge datasets |\n",
    "| Flexible           | NLP, vision, audio       |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Disadvantages\n",
    "\n",
    "| Problem            | Explanation                       |\n",
    "| ------------------ | --------------------------------- |\n",
    "| High memory use    | Attention matrix large            |\n",
    "| Expensive          | Large compute requirements        |\n",
    "| Needs lots of data | Huge models require huge datasets |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Transformer vs RNN\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature           | RNN     | Transformer    |\n",
    "| ----------------- | ------- | -------------- |\n",
    "| Parallelization   | No      | Yes            |\n",
    "| Long-range memory | Weak    | Strong         |\n",
    "| Training speed    | Slow    | Fast           |\n",
    "| Attention         | Limited | Core mechanism |\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine a classroom discussion. Each student:\n",
    "\n",
    "* listens to all others\n",
    "* decides who is important\n",
    "* combines information\n",
    "\n",
    "That is essentially self-attention.\n",
    "\n",
    "A Transformer:\n",
    "\n",
    "* processes sequences using attention\n",
    "* learns relationships between words\n",
    "* handles long contexts efficiently\n",
    "* enables parallel training\n",
    "* powers modern generative AI\n",
    "\n",
    "> Attention rather than recurrence.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Popular Transformer Variants\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model                    | Purpose            |\n",
    "| ------------------------ | ------------------ |\n",
    "| BERT                     | Understanding text |\n",
    "| GPT                      | Text generation    |\n",
    "| T5                       | General NLP        |\n",
    "| Vision Transformer (ViT) | Images             |\n",
    "| Transformer-XL           | Long sequences     |\n",
    "\n",
    "# BERT\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT stands for **Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers**. It is a deep learning language model introduced by Google AI researchers in 2018\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT changed Natural Language Processing (NLP) because it could understand language **contextually and bidirectionally**.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why BERT Was Important\n",
    "\n",
    "Before BERT, many NLP models read text:\n",
    "\n",
    "* left → right  \n",
    "  OR\n",
    "* right → left\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"The bank of the river\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "To understand “bank,” we need both:\n",
    "\n",
    "* previous words\n",
    "* future words\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT reads:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "left + right context simultaneously\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "This made language understanding much better.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Core Idea of BERT\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT is based on the **Transformer Encoder** architecture.\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike GPT:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Uses    |\n",
    "| ----- | ------- |\n",
    "| GPT   | Decoder |\n",
    "| BERT  | Encoder |\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT only uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Transformer Encoder Stack\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Architecture of BERT\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT pipeline:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Input Text\n",
    "2. Tokenization\n",
    "3. Embeddings\n",
    "4. Transformer Encoder Layers\n",
    "5. Contextual Representations\n",
    "6. Task Output\n",
    "\n",
    "**Main Components of BERT**\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Component             | Purpose                  |\n",
    "| --------------------- | ------------------------ |\n",
    "| Token Embeddings      | Represent words          |\n",
    "| Segment Embeddings    | Distinguish sentences    |\n",
    "| Positional Embeddings | Preserve word order      |\n",
    "| Transformer Encoders  | Learn context            |\n",
    "| Self-Attention        | Understand relationships |\n",
    "\n",
    "### BERT Input Representation\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT combines 3 embeddings:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Final Embedding = Token + Position + Segment\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example Input**\n",
    "\n",
    "Sentence pair:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Sentence A: \"I love AI\"\n",
    "Sentence B: \"It is powerful\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT formats input like:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "[CLS] I love AI [SEP] It is powerful [SEP]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Special Tokens**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Token  | Meaning                  |\n",
    "| ------ | ------------------------ |\n",
    "| [CLS]  | Classification token     |\n",
    "| [SEP]  | Separator token          |\n",
    "| [MASK] | Hidden word for training |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Tokenization in BERT\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "#### WordPiece Tokenization\n",
    "\n",
    "Unknown words are split into subwords.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"playing\" → [\"play\", \"##ing\"]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Benefits:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Handles rare words\n",
    "* Smaller vocabulary\n",
    "* Better generalization\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Positional Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "Transformers process tokens in parallel.\n",
    "\n",
    "So BERT adds position information.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Token | Position |\n",
    "| ----- | -------- |\n",
    "| [CLS] | 0        |\n",
    "| I     | 1        |\n",
    "| love  | 2        |\n",
    "| AI    | 3        |"
   ]
