   "source": [
    "## BERT Training Process\n",
    "\n",
    "Steps:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Massive text corpus\n",
    "2. Mask random words\n",
    "3. Predict masked tokens\n",
    "4. Predict sentence relationships\n",
    "5. Update weights using backpropagation\n",
    "\n",
    "Datasets used originally:\n",
    "\n",
    "* BooksCorpus\n",
    "* English Wikipedia\n",
    "\n",
    "### Example of Contextual Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "Traditional embeddings:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"bank\" always same vector\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT embeddings:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"river bank\" ≠ \"money bank\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "because context changes representation.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Example Walkthrough\n",
    "\n",
    "Sentence:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"The movie was surprisingly good.\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Tokenization\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "[\"[CLS]\", \"the\", \"movie\", \"was\", \"surprisingly\", \"good\", \"[SEP]\"]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "Each token converted to vectors.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"movie\" → [0.12, -0.44, 0.88, ...]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Attention\n",
    "\n",
    "Word “good” attends strongly to:\n",
    "\n",
    "* movie\n",
    "* surprisingly\n",
    "\n",
    "to determine sentiment.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Final Representation\n",
    "\n",
    "The `[CLS]` token now summarizes the sentence.\n",
    "\n",
    "Used for:\n",
    "\n",
    "* classification\n",
    "* sentiment analysis\n",
    "* spam detection\n",
    "\n",
    "## Fine-Tuning BERT\n",
    "\n",
    "One of BERT’s biggest strengths:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Fine-tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "Pretrained BERT can adapt to many tasks.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Common Tasks**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Task                     | Example               |\n",
    "| ------------------------ | --------------------- |\n",
    "| Sentiment Analysis       | Positive/negative     |\n",
    "| Question Answering       | Reading comprehension |\n",
    "| Named Entity Recognition | Detect names          |\n",
    "| Text Classification      | Spam detection        |\n",
    "| Search                   | Semantic ranking      |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Sentiment Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Input:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"I absolutely loved this phone.\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT output:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Label    | Probability |\n",
    "| -------- | ----------- |\n",
    "| Positive | 0.97        |\n",
    "| Negative | 0.03        |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Question Answering\n",
    "\n",
    "Context:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"Paris is the capital of France.\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Question:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"What is the capital of France?\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT predicts:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"Paris\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Charecterstics\n",
    "\n",
    "### BERT Variants\n",
    "\n",
    "| Variant    | Description            |\n",
    "| ---------- | ---------------------- |\n",
    "| RoBERTa    | Improved BERT training |\n",
    "| DistilBERT | Smaller/faster         |\n",
    "| ALBERT     | Parameter-efficient    |\n",
    "| TinyBERT   | Lightweight            |\n",
    "| BioBERT    | Biomedical text        |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "| Advantage                     | Explanation            |\n",
    "| ----------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n",
    "| Bidirectional understanding   | Better context         |\n",
    "| Transfer learning             | Fine-tune easily       |\n",
    "| Strong language understanding | Excellent NLP accuracy |\n",
    "| Contextual embeddings         | Dynamic meanings       |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "| Limitation          | Reason                   |\n",
    "| ------------------- | ------------------------ |\n",
    "| Expensive training  | Huge model               |\n",
    "| Slow inference      | Many parameters          |\n",
    "| Input length limits | Usually 512 tokens       |\n",
    "| Encoder-only        | Not ideal for generation |\n",
    "\n",
    "### BERT vs GPT\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature       | BERT           | GPT           |\n",
    "| ------------- | -------------- | ------------- |\n",
    "| Direction     | Bidirectional  | Left-to-right |\n",
    "| Architecture  | Encoder        | Decoder       |\n",
    "| Best For      | Understanding  | Generation    |\n",
    "| Example Tasks | Classification | Writing       |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Real-World Uses\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT powers:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Application            | Example           |\n",
    "| ---------------------- | ----------------- |\n",
    "| Search engines         | Google Search     |\n",
    "| Chatbots               | NLP assistants    |\n",
    "| Recommendation systems | Semantic matching |\n",
    "| Healthcare NLP         | Medical documents |\n",
    "| Finance                | Document analysis |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Intuitive Analogy\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine reading a sentence while covering one word:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"The sky is [MASK].\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "You can guess:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"blue\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "because you understand surrounding context.\n",
    "\n",
    "That is essentially how BERT learns language.\n",
    "\n",
    "BERT is:\n",
    "\n",
    "* a Transformer-based encoder model\n",
    "* deeply bidirectional\n",
    "* trained using masked words\n",
    "* excellent for language understanding tasks\n",
    "\n",
    "Core innovations:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Bidirectional context\n",
    "2. Masked Language Modeling\n",
    "3. Transformer self-attention\n",
    "\n",
    "# GPT\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT stands for **Generative Pre-trained Transformer**. GPT is a family of deep learning language models designed mainly for:\n",
    "\n",
    "* text generation\n",
    "* conversation\n",
    "* summarization\n",
    "* coding\n",
    "* reasoning\n",
    "* question answering\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT models are developed by OpenAI which is based on the **Transformer Decoder architecture**.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why GPT Was Created\n",
    "\n",
    "Earlier NLP systems had limitations:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Problem                    | Explanation            |\n",
    "| -------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n",
    "| Weak context understanding | Limited memory         |\n",
    "| Task-specific training     | Needed separate models |\n",
    "| Poor text generation       | Unnatural outputs      |\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT solved this using:\n",
    "\n",
    "* massive pretraining\n",
    "* Transformer attention\n",
    "* autoregressive generation\n",
    "\n",
    "## Core Idea of GPT\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT learns language by predicting: `What comes next?`\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"The cat sat on the ...\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT predicts:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"mat\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "After predicting “mat”:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"The cat sat on the mat\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "then predicts the next word again. This process continues repeatedly.\n",
    "\n",
    "## GPT Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT uses only Transformer Decoder Blocks\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike BERT:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Architecture |\n",
    "| ----- | ------------ |\n",
    "| BERT  | Encoder      |\n",
    "| GPT   | Decoder      |\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT pipeline:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Input Tokens\n",
    "2. Embeddings\n",
    "3. Masked Self-Attention\n",
    "4. Feed Forward Layers\n",
    "5. Next Token Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "**Important Components**\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Component             | Purpose               |\n",
    "| --------------------- | --------------------- |\n",
    "| Token Embeddings      | Represent words       |\n",
    "| Positional Embeddings | Preserve order        |\n",
    "| Masked Self-Attention | Context understanding |\n",
    "| Feed Forward Networks | Learn transformations |\n",
    "| Softmax Output        | Predict next token    |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Tokenization\n",
    "\n",
    "GPT converts text into tokens.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"Transformers are amazing\"\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "may become:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "[\"Transform\", \"ers\", \" are\", \" amazing\"]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Modern GPT models often use:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Byte Pair Encoding (BPE)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "Each token becomes a vector.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"cat\" → [0.21, -0.44, 0.77, ...]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "These vectors capture semantic meaning."
